From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 02:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: complete restart reconfiguration without open interfaces

ieee80211_restart_hw() marks the hardware as being reconfigured before it
queues the restart worker. If all interfaces are closed before that worker
runs, ieee80211_reconfig() skips driver start as expected. It also skips
the reconfig_complete callback. Drivers which retain recovery state until
that callback then remain stuck in recovery indefinitely.

Call reconfig_complete when an explicit hardware restart is in progress,
even if there are no open interfaces. Keep the open-count check for other
reconfiguration paths so this does not add callbacks to an idle device
outside ieee80211_restart_hw().

This is a narrower adaptation of Qualcomm's downstream SSR recovery fix.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 net/mac80211/util.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/mac80211/util.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/util.c
@@ -2325,7 +2325,8 @@ int ieee80211_reconfig(struct ieee80211_
 	 * If this is for hw restart things are still running.
 	 * We may want to change that later, however.
 	 */
-	if (local->open_count && (!suspended || reconfig_due_to_wowlan))
+	if ((local->open_count || local->in_reconfig) &&
+	    (!suspended || reconfig_due_to_wowlan))
 		drv_reconfig_complete(local, IEEE80211_RECONFIG_TYPE_RESTART);
 
 	if (local->in_reconfig) {
